WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/features/settings/components/AIFeatureToggleList.tsx — a controlled settings list:
    • Generated by mapping over the canonical AI feature registry (`AI_FEATURE_IDS` + `AI_FEATURES` from
      web/src/ai/features.ts, itself generated from internal/ai/features/registry.go) — NEVER hand-listed.
    • Props: `values: Record<AiFeatureId, boolean>` + `onToggle(id, value)`. The component is presentational;
      the Settings page owns the data + the persistence.
    • Each row = `<Subhead>` legend + per feature { medium label, `<Caption>` description, label-less
      `<Toggle aria-label={label} />` }. The switch checked-state is `Boolean(values[id])` (absent ⇒ OFF —
      the legend's "all default off" contract).
    • i18n: legend = `t('ai.settings.feature.legend', 'Per-feature opt-in (all default off)')`; each row
      `t('ai.settings.feature.<id>.label', meta.name)` / `t('ai.settings.feature.<id>.description',
      meta.description)` — i.e. the registry name/description is the fallback so a newly registered feature
      renders before its translations land. No async loading/error/empty states exist in the web source.

ARTIFACTS SHIPPED  (allowed files: apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/AIFeatureToggleList.* + this log)
  AIFeatureToggleList.Adapter.swift     — pure Foundation core: the AIFeatureToggleEntry registry DTO (only
                                          id/name/description, the fields the surface reads), the
                                          AIFeatureToggleRow view-ready row, the AIFeatureToggleConnection
                                          freshness axis, the AIFeatureToggleAdapter.row(...) resolver (i18n
                                          key derivation + registry fallback + `Boolean(values[id])` value
                                          lookup, parameterised on a translate closure so it is bundle-free
                                          testable), and AIFeatureToggleAccessibility.
  AIFeatureToggleList.Projection.swift  — pure AIFeatureToggleProjection.resolve: error → loading → empty →
                                          data; builds the legend + the registry-ordered rows.
